WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.030
You can't keep a good scoundrel down.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:07.260
Han Solo might have died in The Force Awakens,
but the character lives on in film thanks

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:12.889
to the spinoff prequel Solo: A Star Wars Story,
which features Alden Ehrenreich as the galaxy's

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:14.280
scruffiest nerf herder.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.380
But with more than 40 years of Star Wars history
to draw on, Solo's many references and easter

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.770
eggs could be daunting for fans both young
and old.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.510
Don't worry: we have you covered.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.600
Here's what you need to know before you see
Solo: A Star Wars Story.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.640
When does Solo take place?

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.660
Going by the timeline established in the official
tie-in novel Last Shot, the action in Solo

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:40.270
appears to take place somewhere between three
and eight years before the events of A New

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.270
Hope.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:44.980
So don't expect to see familiar faces like
Leia and Luke, because at this point in his

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.000
young career, Han is a one-man operation.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.420
That's going to change, though, as the film
promises to show Han's meeting with his right-hand-Wookiee

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:57.120
Chewbacca, as well as the galaxy's smoothest
frenemy, Lando Calrissian.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.200
And that leads to the infamous game of cards
that wins Han his one true love, the Millennium

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:07.140
Falcon, a game first mentioned way back in
1980's The Empire Strikes Back.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.860
"What have you done to my ship?"

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.860
"YOUR ship?

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.520
Hey… remember you lost her to me, fair and
square."

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.740
Who is the Game of Thrones lady playing?

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.860
Game of Thrones viewers know her best as Daenerys
Targaryen, the Mother of Dragons, but in Solo,

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:26.390
actress Emilia Clarke plays a very different
yet equally badass lady in the form of Han's

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.820
sometimes partner-in-crime Qi'ra.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.450
She may look glamorous, but Clarke assures
fans she's just as devious as Solo himself.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:34.450
She explained:

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:38.580
"If you have got a really glamorous lady in
a really sordid environment, you kind of know

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.939
that maybe the glamour is hiding a few rough
roads.

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:45.700
[…] The thing that that you see with Qi'ra
is that she an enigma."

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.870
Who is L3-37?

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:52.960
In the grand Star Wars tradition, Solo will
introduce a new droid to the Star Wars universe.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:57.240
But some parts of Lando's partner L3-37 will
look familiar to fans.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.330
Literally: the droid is self-made, having
constructed herself out of spare parts from

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:06.530
other droid models, including bits of BB and
R2 units, and protocol droids like C-3PO.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.879
And in the Last Shot novel, we learn that
L3 is both a committed droids' rights activist

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:14.270
and deeply spiritual, saying in the book,

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:18.890
"Some guy in a factory probably pieced me
together originally, and someone else programmed

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:19.890
me.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.790
But then the galaxy itself forged me into
who I am.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:23.969
Because we learn.

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:28.120
[…] Maybe we're our own makers, no matter
who put the parts together."

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.099
Who are the new rogues?

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:34.419
Though Solo has plenty of cameos and callbacks,
most of the supporting characters are all

00:02:34.419 --> 00:02:35.779
new to the Star Wars universe.

00:02:35.779 --> 00:02:40.419
So you don't need to read or watch anything
in order to appreciate Woody Harrelson's criminal

00:02:40.419 --> 00:02:46.159
mentor Tobias Beckett, Thandie Newton's expert
marksman Val, or Paul Bettany's crime boss

00:02:46.159 --> 00:02:47.579
Dryden Vos.

00:02:47.579 --> 00:02:51.859
Fans of the Star Wars comics from Dark Horse
are in for a treat, though, as Jonathan Kasdan

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:57.129
and Toby Hefferman, Solo's co-writer and assistant
director respectively, portray Imperial soldiers

00:02:57.129 --> 00:03:01.889
Tag and Bink, bumbling officials who accidentally
play a key role behind the scenes throughout

00:03:01.889 --> 00:03:03.580
the original trilogy.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.920
Classic.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.840
Where's the fan service?

00:03:06.859 --> 00:03:10.879
While the whole film could be considered fan
service, there are more inside references

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:13.129
than just the inclusion of Tag and Bink.

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:18.180
For instance, part of Solo is set on the mud
planet of Mimban, which was originally introduced

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.799
was back in the 1978 tie-in novel Splinter
of the Mind's Eye, but it's never made it

00:03:22.799 --> 00:03:24.930
into an actual movie until now.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.180
And the tease of other Wookiees could signal
the return of Chewie's family.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:34.739
Though most fans would prefer to forget it,
the 1978 Star Wars Holiday Special introduced

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:37.519
Chewbacca's wife Malla and his son Lumpy.

00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:42.419
Bringing them back would be the ultimate inside
nod for hardcore Star Wars fans.

00:03:42.419 --> 00:03:44.459
Who directed this thing, anyway?

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:47.959
Rumors of problems on-set plagued Solo right
from the start.

00:03:47.959 --> 00:03:52.709
To help smooth over production woes, Lucasfilm
reportedly hired an acting coach for star

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:57.109
Alden Ehrenreich and brought in co-writer
Lawrence Kasdan, who also co-wrote both Empire

00:03:57.109 --> 00:04:00.870
Strikes Back and Return of the Jedi, to lead
script rewrites.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.720
And when things still didn't get straightened
out, Lucasfilm went with the nuclear option,

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.659
firing directors Phil Lord and Christopher
Miller right in the middle of shooting.

00:04:08.659 --> 00:04:13.319
After a delay of several weeks, Ron Howard
came aboard to finish filming and right the

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.319
ship.

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:18.569
Hey, it wouldn't be a true Han Solo adventure
if everything went according to plan.

00:04:18.569 --> 00:04:19.979
What's the bottom line?

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:24.740
Though Solo is obviously intended to fit into
the greater Star Wars universe, fans don't

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.340
really have to worry about knowing every little
bit of franchise trivia.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:33.259
Because unlike the previous Star Wars films,
Solo is designed to be a totally self-contained

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:34.590
one-shot film.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.020
Sure, you'll get more out of it if you get
some of the in-jokes, but there shouldn't

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:42.400
be any cliffhangers here, just a big, sprawling
space adventure featuring one of the most

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.440
beloved characters in cinema.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.150
That's not to say this is necessarily the
end, though.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:51.680
If Solo ends up being really popular, we might
get more big-screen adventures starring young

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.680
Han.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.800
That's because Alden Ehrenreich is apparently
signed up for three movies.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:59.930
So will the film prove popular enough to spawn
a trilogy of its own?

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:04.880
If there's one thing we've learned over the
years, it's never bet against Han Solo.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:05.880
Thanks for watching!

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.319
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:11.009
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

